# Line endings are LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with the default core.autocrlf=true gets CRLF
# files, and everything that reads them line by line is looking at text nobody
# wrote that way: the docs checker's fence and heading scanning, biome's
# formatter, and any `#!` line, where a trailing CR stops the script from
# starting at all. It also keeps a Windows contributor's first diff from being
# every line of every file.
#
# `text=auto` rather than `text`: git still decides for itself what is binary,
# so this cannot corrupt one.
* text=auto eol=lf
